  "raw_text": "Step 1: The steel sphere is inscribed in the cube, meaning the diameter of the sphere is equal to the side length of the cube.\n\nStep 2: Since the radius of the sphere is 3 inches, its diameter is \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) inches, which is also the side length of the cube.\n\nStep 3: The volume of a cube is given by the formula \\(V = s^3\\), where \\(s\\) is the side length of the cube.\n\nStep 4: Substituting the side length of the cube into the formula gives \\(V = 6^3 = 216\\) cubic inches.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{216}<|im_end|>",
